# 高频词汇 List02
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List02核心词汇

{{identify}}{/aɪˈdentɪfaɪ/}{识别；确认}{The police identified the suspect from the footage.}
{{illustrate}}{/ˈɪləstreɪt/}{说明；插图}{The graph illustrates the trend clearly.}
{{impact}}{/ˈɪmpækt/}{影响；冲击}{The policy had a significant impact on education.}
{{implement}}{/ˈɪmplɪment/}{实施；执行}{The government plans to implement new regulations.}}
{{implication}}{/ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃn/}{含义；暗示}{The implications of this study are far-reaching.}
{{impose}}{/ɪmˈpəʊz/}{施加；强加}{The new law imposes stricter penalties on offenders.}
{{incentive}}{/ɪnˈsentɪv/}{激励；动机}{Financial incentives can boost productivity.}}
{{indicate}}{/ˈɪndɪkeɪt/}{表明；指示}{Research indicates that exercise improves mental health.}}
{{individual}}{/ˌɪndɪˈvɪdʒuəl/}{个人的；个体}{Each individual has unique talents.}}
{{inevitable}}{/ɪnˈevɪtəbl/}{不可避免的}{Change is inevitable in a rapidly developing world.}}
{{influence}}{/ˈɪnfluəns/}{影响；势力}{Parents have a great influence on their children.}}
{{initial}}{/ɪˈnɪʃl/}{最初的；开始的}{The initial results were very promising.}}
{{innovation}}{/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃn/}{创新；革新}{Innovation drives economic growth.}}
{{insight}}{/ˈɪnsaɪt/}{洞察力；见解}{The book offers valuable insights into human behavior.}}
{{instance}}{/ˈɪnstəns/}{实例；情况}{In this instance, the judge ruled in favor of the defendant.}}
{{institution}}{/ˌɪnstɪˈtjuːʃn/}{机构；制度}{Universities are important educational institutions.}}
{{integrate}}{/ˈɪntɪɡreɪt/}{整合；融入}{The company aims to integrate new technology into its products.}}
{{intellectual}}{/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəl/}{智力的；知识分子}{Intellectual property protection is crucial for innovation.}}
{{intend}}{/ɪnˈtend/}{打算；意图}{I intend to finish this project by Friday.}}
{{interact}}{/ˌɪntərˈækt/}{互动；相互作用}{Students learn better when they interact with each other.}}
{{interpret}}{/ɪnˈtɜːprɪt/}{解释；翻译}{Different cultures interpret this gesture differently.}}
{{intervene}}{/ˌɪntəˈviːn/}{干预；介入}{The government decided to intervene in the crisis.}}
{{investigate}}{/ɪnˈvestɪɡeɪt/}{调查；研究}{The police are investigating the cause of the accident.}}
{{involve}}{/ɪnˈvɒlv/}{涉及；包含}{The project involves collaboration between multiple departments.}}
{{isolate}}{/ˈaɪsəleɪt/}{隔离；孤立}{Scientists isolated the virus in the laboratory.}}
{{issue}}{/ˈɪʃuː/}{问题；发行}{Climate change is a pressing issue worldwide.}}
{{justify}}{/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ/}{证明...正当}{Can you justify your decision with evidence?}}
{{label}}{/ˈleɪbl/}{标签；贴标签}{Don't judge people by the labels society puts on them.}}
{{launch}}{/lɔːntʃ/}{发射；启动}{The company launched a new product line last month.}}
{{legitimate}}{/lɪˈdʒɪtɪmət/}{合法的；正当的}{The business operates in a legitimate manner.}}
